1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,616
Every founder knows this moment.

2
00:00:02,616 --> 00:00:03,476
It's nine p.

3
00:00:03,476 --> 00:00:03,608
m.

4
00:00:03,608 --> 00:00:06,716
, you're out for dinner, and your phone buzzes.

5
00:00:06,716 --> 00:00:08,104
A refund to approve.

6
00:00:08,104 --> 00:00:09,294
A vendor waiting.

7
00:00:09,294 --> 00:00:10,484
A calendar clash.

8
00:00:10,484 --> 00:00:15,311
Small decisions, but your whole team is stuck until you open the laptop.

9
00:00:16,611 --> 00:00:19,521
This is Greenlight, an approval terminal for Even G2.

10
00:00:19,521 --> 00:00:26,878
Requests from Telegram, Gmail and Google Calendar arrive on your glasses as one card, already checked against your own company rules.

11
00:00:28,178 --> 00:00:29,097
Set it up once.

12
00:00:29,097 --> 00:00:32,898
Connect your accounts, and write your rules in plain English.

13
00:00:32,898 --> 00:00:35,473
Flag expenses above five hundred dollars.

14
00:00:35,473 --> 00:00:37,557
Never double-book investor calls.

15
00:00:37,557 --> 00:00:40,377
Then pair your glasses with a six-digit code.

16
00:00:41,677 --> 00:00:47,269
Rohan, from a client team, asks for a three-twenty-dollar AWS refund in Telegram.

17
00:00:47,269 --> 00:00:54,312
Greenlight reads it, checks your rules, and shows one card: what, who, and a one-line recommendation.

18
00:00:54,312 --> 00:00:55,693
One tap to approve.

19
00:00:55,693 --> 00:00:57,833
You get three seconds to undo.

20
00:00:57,833 --> 00:01:02,183
Then it's done, and Rohan sees the approval right in the chat.

21
00:01:03,483 --> 00:01:05,263
Not everything is a green light.

22
00:01:05,263 --> 00:01:08,321
A nine-hundred-dollar vendor invoice arrives by email.

23
00:01:08,321 --> 00:01:11,881
Greenlight flags it, because it's over your five-hundred limit.

24
00:01:11,881 --> 00:01:15,551
Hold to decline, and a polite reply goes back on the same thread.

25
00:01:16,851 --> 00:01:19,547
A new invite clashes with your investor call.

26
00:01:19,547 --> 00:01:22,961
Greenlight flags it against your no-double-booking rule.

27
00:01:22,961 --> 00:01:25,237
Decline it, and the calendar updates.

28
00:01:26,537 --> 00:01:31,938
Every tap is logged: who asked, what for, the policy verdict, your decision, and when.

29
00:01:31,938 --> 00:01:35,079
Open the dashboard, and the whole trail is there.

30
00:01:36,379 --> 00:01:37,027
Greenlight.

31
00:01:37,027 --> 00:01:38,089
Read the request.

32
00:01:38,089 --> 00:01:39,151
Trust your rules.

33
00:01:39,151 --> 00:01:40,271
Decide in one tap.
